  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Evidence-based research to inform policy decision making in PFM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will contribute towards improved use and management of public resources through a public financial management system that promotes transparency, accountability, fiscal discipline, efficiency and effectiveness by enhancing decision making and multi -stakeholder debates on PFM issues, enabled by a robust evidence -based research and sharing of best practice models. The project will enhance analysis and expand an inclusive civic space that enables policy influencing and active citizenship in public finance management for great efficiency and cost reduction in public service delivery. Oxfam in Malawi will work with Economics Association of Malawi (ECAMA) and Lilongwe University of Agriculture and Natural Resources (LUANAR) through establishment of research teams to analyse available information and anecdotal case studies on PFM to propose viable policy options for public discussion and consideration at the appropriate level of decision making in public finance management system for better targeted policies and poverty reduction. The action will not focus not exclusively on PFM at central but also at local level by analysing available information and PFM trends in, ten districts of Rumphi, Mzimba, Dowa, Mchinji, Kasungu, Phalombe, Balaka, Mangochi, Zomba and Machinga. It is expected that information from these districts would prompt the public to get engaged with deliberations and debate on PFM issues by bringing real life stories on the impact of poor public finance management in service delivery.</narrative>
  </description>
